{
  "id": "ss.fx.cut",
  "name": "Cut",
  "description": "Where a blade of yours crossed a body: three thin slivers laid along the line of the stroke, crossing at a shallow angle, on a sliver of ink each a hair wider. Drawn pointing +x — the engine turns it to the stroke's tangent — and baked rather than drawn live, because there are many of them and they are all the same size. It flicks out long, holds, thins to a line and goes, in a tenth of a second and a half: the cut is the shape of the stroke, not a burst, so a Lash's strike reads as a slice and a crit's Shell break (ss.fx.impact) reads as something else. Frost-white on the cold side of the palette, never the hive's pink; the player's marks do not glow.",
